# SWYNEX Final Data Analytics Project

## Project Overview
This project analyzes Superstore Sales data to understand sales performance, profitability, and business trends.

## Problem Statement
- The objective of this project is to analyze Superstore sales and profit data to identify sales trends, profitable product categories, high-performing regions and products that generate losses.
- The analysis aims to identify opportunities to improve profitability and support better business decisions.


## Dataset Information
- Dataset: Superstore Sales
- Total Records: 9,994
- Period: 2014–2017

## Tools Used
- Microsoft Excel
- Microsoft Power BI

## Project Tasks

### Task 1: Data Cleaning
Cleaned and prepared the dataset for analysis.

### Task 2: Exploratory Data Analysis
Analyzed sales, profit, categories, regions, and other business trends using Excel.

### Task 3: Power BI Dashboard
Created an interactive dashboard with 4 KPI cards, 6 charts, and 6 slicers.

### Task 4: Complete Analytics Case Study
Prepared a final report covering the problem statement, dataset information, Data cleaning and prepartion, EDA analysis, POWER BI dashboard, and key business insights.

## Key Business Insights
-	Technology was the highest-selling product category.
-	The West region recorded the highest sales among the regions in the analysis.
- The Consumer segment contributed the highest sales.
- Sales increased between 2014 and 2017.
- Tables and Bookcases recorded negative profits.
- High discounts were associated with significant losses in some transactions.
- Shipping performance can be monitored using the shipping-mode and average-shipping-days analysis.


## Project Deliverables
- Cleaned Superstore Sales dataset
-	EDA Analysis 
- Power BI Superstore Sales and Profit Analysis Dashboard
- Final Data Analytics Project report
- Final Data Analytics Project video 

## Conclusion
This project helped me develop practical skills in data cleaning, data analysis, data visualization, and dashboard creation.

